  "Question": "The lines satisfy \\(l_1\\parallel l_2\\parallel l_3\\). Line \\(a\\) intersects \\(l_1\\), \\(l_2\\), and \\(l_3\\) at \\(A\\), \\(B\\), and \\(C\\), respectively. Line \\(b\\) intersects \\(l_1\\), \\(l_2\\), and \\(l_3\\) at \\(D\\), \\(E\\), and \\(F\\), respectively. If \\(AB=3\\), \\(BC=6\\), and \\(DE=4\\), find \\(EF\\).",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "8",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "When three parallel lines intersect two lines, the corresponding segments are proportional: \\(AB/BC=DE/EF\\), or \\(3/6=4/EF\\). Therefore, \\(EF=8\\).",
